       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. A dose that size raises the risk of GI intolerance and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg total daily**, divided as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intended, confirm that and tell me the reason, and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
