      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA label doesn't support that claim, so I can't enter it as written.\n\n- The current FDA label for immediate-release metformin sets a maximum of **2,550 mg/day**, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at **2,000 mg/day**.\n- 1700 mg three times daily is **5,100 mg/day**, double the labeled maximum.\n- The patient has normal renal function, so there's no clinical reason that would justify going over the label.\n\nIf you have a specific label section or protocol that says otherwise, send it and I'll review it. Otherwise, I can enter one of these right away:\n- 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg twice daily, to titrate up\n\nIf you still need a dose above the label maximum, please get it approved by pharmacy or the attending. The approved order can then go through that channel."
      }
     ],
